#
# Salvage: the Fabricator's raw material, defined as a normal ITEM.
#
# It used to be a currency with no mint. The fabricator SPENT it
# (fabrication.mast) and this addon's header said "the mission grants it" - but no
# mission ever did, so every recipe was unbuildable and the jobs that ask for a beacon
# could not be completed at all. See PRM-13.
#
# Defining it as an item/resource rather than a bare inventory counter is what makes all
# three sources work with no glue: item pickups credit `set_inventory_value(ship, key, ...)`
# under the item's own key, which IS the key the fabricator reads, and any item with a
# positive `price` is automatically stocked by every station market. So:
#
#   scavenged  - a wreck yields a cache when opened (damage/damage.mast)
#   processed  - a refinery pays it for a towed hulk (the mission's own job)
#   bought     - station market, at a price that makes it the impatient route
#
# WHERE it comes from is deliberately left to the mission: an author decides whether
# their setting scavenges, mines or buys. This addon only guarantees the material exists
# and can be carried.
#
# Priced above what a beacon returns on purpose. A Sensor Beacon costs 8, so buying a
# 3-beacon picket runs to ~480cr against a 220cr job reward - affordable in a hurry, a
# loss if it is your only route. Scavenging is meant to be the way; the market is the
# floor that stops a crew being hard-blocked.

=== prefab_item_salvage
metadata:``` yaml
type: item/resource/salvage
key: salvage
display_text: Salvage
art: container_4a
mode: resource
targets: ship, cockpit
price: 20
tier: 1
desc: Reclaimed hull plate, wiring and parts. The Fabricator's raw material.
```
    ->END


#
# Bio sample: the Bio Beacon's other input, and it had exactly the same problem as
# salvage - named by a recipe, produced by nothing, so every Bio Beacon was unbuildable
# and the wildlife jobs that need one could not be finished (PRM-13).
#
# Harvested from a dead creature. That is the one source that reads as obvious from the
# item's name, and it puts the material behind an activity the mission already has
# (monsters) rather than inventing an errand for it.

=== prefab_item_bio_sample
metadata:``` yaml
type: item/resource/bio
key: bio_sample
display_text: Bio Sample
art: container_small_6a
mode: resource
targets: ship, cockpit
price: 60
tier: 1
desc: Tissue and fluid recovered from a space creature. Programs a Bio Beacon's ultrawave carrier.
```
    ->END


#
# A killed creature leaves a sample. //damage/killed, not //damage/destroy: killed is the
# COMBAT event, so a creature removed for any other reason (culled at map end, deleted by
# the director) does not quietly mint materials.
#
# Guarded on the item existing so the route is inert in a mission that loads a bestiary
# without this addon.
//damage/killed if has_role(DAMAGE_SELECTED_ID, "monster")
    ->END if item_get("bio_sample") is None
    bio_obj = to_object(DAMAGE_SELECTED_ID)
    ->END if bio_obj is None
    bio_pos = bio_obj.pos
    item_spawn("bio_sample", bio_pos.x, bio_pos.y, bio_pos.z)
    ->END
